[0m[K [38;5;248mShould I complete the goal? The goal tool instructions say complete only when verified done. The deliverable is the PM_RESULT line in my response. After emitting it, the task is complete. But can I call goal({op:"complete"}) and then emit the line? The constraint says "Use no ordinary tools" — that refers to ordinary tools like file access/bash. The goal tool is part of goal-mode management. The instruction says use no ordinary tools and do not access files. The goal tool isn't an ordinary     [0m
 [38;5;248mtool; it's the mode manager. However, calling goal complete before yielding the result... The order: I should produce the final answer with PM_RESULT line as the last nonempty line. If I call goal({op:"complete"}) via tool call, then the tool result comes back, and then I write my final message containing the PM_RESULT line. That works.[39m                                                                                                                                                                 [0m
