                                                                                                                                                              [0m[54;1H[0m[K [38;5;248mWait — order issue: should goal completion happen before emitting the result? The goal tool description: complete marks goal complete only when actually done and every deliverable verified. At the time of the call, the deliverable (PM_RESULT line) hasn't been emitted yet. Hmm. Strictly, the deliverable is emitted after. Is that a problem? The instruction says complete only when actually done. Calling complete right before emitting the final line is standard practice in these goal-mode setups — [0m[55;1H[0m[K [38;5;248mthe completion call signals intent, then final answer. Alternatively, emit PM_RESULT in message 1, then call goal complete in message 2, then message 3 would be empty-ish... can't have empty final message; and final nonempty line must be PM_RESULT — if message 3 needs content, repeating PM_RESULT violates "exactly one PM_RESULT line"? It says "the final nonempty line must be exactly one PM_RESULT [39;38;5;248m<minified JSON>[39;38;5;248m line" — exactly one such line total presumably. So repeating is bad.[39m               [0m[56;1H                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    [0m[57;1H [38;5;248mBest: Message 1: explanation + tool call (goal complete). Message 2: PM_RESULT line alone. This keeps exactly one PM_RESULT line, as the final nonempty line of the entire reply sequence.[39m                          